; C = A * B on row-major square matrices, as clang -O2 -fno-vectorize
; -fno-unroll-loops emits it (test/MAIR/TestCases/{asan,tsan}/mair-matmul.c
; is the source). default<O1> folds every loop level and leaves three
; observations in the function entry graph: one write of all of C and one
; read each of all of A and all of B.
;
; - A[i][k] over k is the row [A + 4ni, + 4n), C[i][j] over j the row
;   [C + 4ni, + 4n). The i loop advances each row by its size, so the rows abut.
; - B[k][j] over k is a column: periodic with start B + 4j, stride 4n, access
;   size 4, n trips. The j loop advances the start by 4 and n * 4 is the
;   stride, so the columns fill [B, + 4n^2). It does not depend on i, so it
;   is hoisted out of the i loop.

; for (i < 64) for (j < 64) { s = 0; for (k < 64) s += A[i][k] * B[k][j]; C[i][j] = s; }
